 **Review the seeded prefixes with the user.** Nothing is mapped until `srm-sync` runs, so this is the free moment to override. Show the seeded entries as a table (name → prefix → path → layout) and ask whether the prefixes are acceptable. If the user wants a different prefix, edit `prefix:` for that entry in `sources.yaml` — a plain rename at this stage costs nothing because no `<prefix>-*` skills exist yet. Do not run `srm-sync` as part of setup; mapping is the user's explicit next step.
 
+**Check which seeds are already cloned.** Resolve `{skills_repo_root}` from the config just written and stat each seeded `path`. Report plainly — "2 of 6 sources cloned locally" — and if any are missing, tell the user `srm-sync` will clone the rest on demand (`--clone-missing` fetches each via its registry `url`; a plain `srm-sync` lists them as `missing` and offers the same). This sets expectations for a fresh workspace, where typically none exist yet.
+
 The registry maps external repos to this project: `path` (may use the `{skills_repo_root}` token), the user-chosen `prefix`, `layout` (`grouped` = BMad source modules, `flat` = dir of SKILL.md folders), `git_pull`, and `skills_paths`. Users manage it afterwards through the `srm-sync` skill (`add`/`remove`/`list`) — never by editing config.yaml.
 
